decision_conditions:
Condition : 14 - No development shall take place on any phase above ground until details and samples of all facing materials to buildings relevant to that phase are submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. 
The samples and details shall include:
A.	Brick materials shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with Barratt London - Planning Condition 14A Discharge Revision 01 April 2017; E1108 W0189 P6; E1108 D0211 P1; E1108 D0212 P1; E1108 D0213 P1; E1108 D0214 P1; E1108 D0215 P1; E1108 D0216 P1; Brick specification document. Received: 19/04/2017 and approved under application 00616/F/P20(14A).
B.	stonework (including brick/stone and mortar on-site sample panel for each building) (where relevant); 
C.	cladding materials (including system specifications/details and on-site samples for each building);
D.	window treatment (including sections/reveals and on-site sample panel for each building);  
E.	obscure glazing details (where relevant); 
F.	balustrading treatment (including sections for each balcony type);
G.	privacy screens (where relevant); 
H.	any other materials/details to be used including extract vents, boiler flues, etc.
Each phase of the development shall then be carried out in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.
